title: Postal Service
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: potus_affairs, cabinet
card-image: img/Post.webp
on-arrival: postmaster_policy_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
view-if: sect_postmaster_party = "R" and postmaster_policy_timer <= 0
go-to: postmaster_policy

= Postmaster General

The Post Office is the largest arm of the federal bureaucracy and the most politically lucrative. With tens of thousands of postal jobs to award, the Postmaster General wields extraordinary patronage power.

@postmaster_policy

- @southern_patronage: Fill Southern postal jobs with loyal Unionists and Black <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span>.
- @machine_loyalty: Reward Northern party men and fundraisers with plum appointments.
- @civil_service_reform: Begin removing patronage and professionalizing the postal service.
- @reform_act: Pass the Civil Service Reform Act and end patronage for good.
- @root: Leave the Post Office on autopilot for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@southern_patronage
subtitle: -1 Budget
on-arrival: freemen_rep += 3; rural_dem -= 2; radical_strength += 1; conservative_dissent += 1; budget -= 1; PoliticalCostPenalty += 1; kkk_strength += 2

Thousands of postal appointments across the South are handed to Black <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span>, Union loyalists, and carpetbaggers. This expands federal presence in the region but inflames local opposition and fuels accusations of corruption.

@machine_loyalty
subtitle: +1 Budget
choose-if: reform_act = 0
unavailable-subtitle: We have abolished such corruption with the Civil Service Reform Act
on-arrival: middle_class_rep += 2; moderate_strength += 1; budget += 1

We funnel high-paying postal appointments to loyal party operators and fundraisers. While it strengthens internal discipline and fundraising, it risks backlash from reformers and independents.

@civil_service_reform
subtitle: -1 Budget
view-if: reform_act = 0
on-arrival: liberal_strength += 1; civil_service_reform += 1; conservative_dissent += 1; budget -= 1

We move to de-politicize the Post Office and institute merit hiring. Though it earns praise from reformers, it angers loyal partisans who expect rewards for service.

@reform_act
subtitle: The <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservatives**</span> will not be pleased.
choose-if: house_majority > 1 and senate_majority > 1
unavailable-subtitle: We don't control Congress.
view-if: civil_service_reform = 3
on-arrival: liberal_strength +=3; liberal_dissent -=5; conservative_dissent +=6; reform_act = 1; middle_class_rep += 1; workers_rep += 3

We have successfully passed the Civil Service Reform Act! Reformers are very pleased with us, but loyal <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservative**</span> party members who are used to receiving rewards are outraged.
